{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,5,14]],"date-time":"2026-05-14T22:16:09Z","timestamp":1778796969217,"version":"3.51.4"},"reference-count":61,"publisher":"American Geophysical Union (AGU)","issue":"8","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2015,8,3]],"date-time":"2015-08-03T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1438560000000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":2,"URL":"http:\/\/onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/termsAndConditions#vor"}],"funder":[{"name":"European Commission as part of the FP7 project ACCESS-Arctic Climate Change, Economy and Society","award":["265863"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["265863"]}]},{"name":"RACE-Regional Atlantic Circulation and Global Change","award":["0F0651 D"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["0F0651 D"]}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["JGR Oceans"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2015,8]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title><jats:p>Time\u2010space varying uncertainty maps of monthly mean Arctic summer ice drift are presented. To assess the error statistics of two low\u2010resolution Eulerian ice drift products, we use high\u2010resolution Lagrangian ice motion derived from synthetic aperture radar (SAR) imagery. The Lagrangian trajectories from the SAR data are converted to an Eulerian format to serve as reference for the error assessment of the Eulerian products. The statistical error associated with the conversion is suppressed to an acceptable level by applying a threshold for averaging. By using the SAR ice drift as a reference, we formulate the uncertainty of monthly mean ice drift as an empirical function of drift speed and ice concentration. The empirical functions are applied to derive uncertainty maps of Arctic ice drift fields. The estimated uncertainty maps reasonably capture an increase of uncertainty with the progress of summer melting season. The uncertainties range from 1.0 to 2.0 cm s<jats:sup>\u22121<\/jats:sup>, which indicates that the low\u2010resolution Eulerian products for summer seasons are of practical use for climate studies, model validation, and data assimilation, if their uncertainties are appropriately taken into account.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1002\/2015jc010810","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2015,6,12]],"date-time":"2015-06-12T16:41:29Z","timestamp":1434127289000},"page":"5285-5301","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":38,"title":["Uncertainty of <scp>A<\/scp>rctic summer ice drift assessed by high\u2010resolution SAR data"],"prefix":"10.1029","volume":"120","author":[{"given":"Hiroshi","family":"Sumata","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Sea Ice Physics Alfred Wegener Institute for Polar and Marine Research Bremerhaven Germany"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Ronald","family":"Kwok","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Jet Propulsion Laboratory California Institute of Technology California USA"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"R\u00fcdiger","family":"Gerdes","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Sea Ice Physics Alfred Wegener Institute for Polar and Marine Research Bremerhaven Germany"},{"name":"Jacobs University Bremen Germany"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Frank","family":"Kauker","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Sea Ice Physics Alfred Wegener Institute for Polar and Marine Research Bremerhaven Germany"},{"name":"Ocean Atmosphere Systems Hamburg Germany"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Michael","family":"Karcher","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Sea Ice Physics Alfred Wegener Institute for Polar and Marine Research Bremerhaven Germany"},{"name":"Ocean Atmosphere Systems Hamburg Germany"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"13","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2015,8,3]]},"reference":[{"key":"e_1_2_8